{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"normalized":[{"from":"Strike_(Watcher)","to":"Strike (Watcher)"},{"from":"Seeing_Red","to":"Seeing Red"},{"from":"Compile_Driver","to":"Compile Driver"},{"from":"Self_Repair","to":"Self Repair"},{"from":"Wild_Strike","to":"Wild Strike"}],"pages":{"1434":{"pageid":1434,"ns":0,"title":"Bash","revisions":[{"revid":56325,"parentid":55638,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Bash\n| Image       = Red-Bash.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Basic\n| Cost        = 2\n| Description = Deal (8;10) damage.<br>Apply (2;3) {{BD|Vulnerable}}.\n| GivesToEnemy = Vulnerable\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Vulnerable}}\n{{C|Bash}} is a 2 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Basic|Basic}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 8 (10 if upgraded) damage and applies 2 (3 if upgraded) {{BD|Vulnerable}} to the target.\n\n== Obtaining Bash ==\nThe [[Ironclad]] starts the game with one copy of {{C|Bash}} in his deck. It cannot be obtained through regular card rewards, but can be obtained in the {{E|Match and Keep}} Event. \n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Paper Phrog}} increases the effectiveness of {{BD|Vulnerable}}.\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2115":{"pageid":2115,"ns":0,"title":"Blizzard","revisions":[{"revid":56902,"parentid":55654,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Blizzard\n|Image       = Blue-Blizzard.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal damage equal to (2;3) times the number of {{KW|Frost}} {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} this combat to ALL enemies.\n|InteractsWith = Channel, Frost\n}}\n{{C|Blizzard}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. <!--It does damage equal to double (triple) the number of {{KW|Frost|Frost Orbs}} {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} this combat to ALL enemies.-->\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Blizzard benefits from all sources of {{KW|Frost|Frost Orbs}}, but especially {{C|Glacier}} and {{C|Chill}}, which can {{KW|Channel}} multiple at once.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* While Blizzard does more damage for each {{KW|Frost|Frost Orb}} {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} this combat, the damage is done as one large hit. As such, it does not scale especially well with {{BD|Strength}} or {{BD|Vigor}}.\n** On the other hand, it also only triggers {{BD|Thorns}} once.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 48: Creative AI'''\n** Blizzard gets improved size, velocity, and SFX pitch scaling logic (now up to 50 Frost).\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 47: Metamorphosis'''\n** Adding VFX for Blizzard Card (scales with Frost channeled).\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 28: The Ritual'''\n** Fixed an issue where Blizzard card was causing crashes in French.\nWeekly Patch 27: Hello World\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1897":{"pageid":1897,"ns":0,"title":"Bludgeon","revisions":[{"revid":50454,"parentid":35980,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Bludgeon\n|Image       = Red-Bludgeon.png\n|Color       = Red\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 3\n|Description = Deal (32;42) damage.\n}}\n{{C|Bludgeon}} is a 3 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 32 (42 if upgraded) damage.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2064":{"pageid":2064,"ns":0,"title":"Compile Driver","revisions":[{"revid":56945,"parentid":56944,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation|1|1}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Compile Driver\n|Image       = Blue-CompileDriver.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (7;10) damage.<br>Draw 1 card for each unique Orb you have.\n|GivesToPlayer = Draw\n|InteractsWith = Orb\n}}\n{{C|Compile Driver}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Cracked Core}}, {{R|Symbiotic Virus}} and {{R|Nuclear Battery}} each give Compile Driver 1 extra draw directly from the start of combat.\n** {{C|Chill|Chill+}} also gives an additional draw always in your starting hand.\n\n* {{C|Rainbow}} gives 3 unique [[Orbs]] by itself, possibly allowing {{C|Compile Driver}} to draw 3 cards. {{C|Chaos}} can also {{KW|Channel}} unique Orbs, but unreliably.\n\n* {{C|Capacitor}}, {{R|Runic Capacitor}}, {{R|Inserter}}, and {{P|Potion of Capacity}} give additional Orb Slots, allowing Compile Driver to draw up to 4 cards, as well as making it easier to keep multiple Orb types {{KW|Channel|Channeled}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2070":{"pageid":2070,"ns":0,"title":"Coolheaded","revisions":[{"revid":56948,"parentid":55706,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Coolheaded\n|Image       = Blue-Coolheaded.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = {{KW|Channel}} 1 {{KW|Frost}}.<br>Draw (1;2) (card;cards).\n|GivesToPlayer = Draw, Channel, Frost\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Frost}}\n{{C|Coolheaded}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. <!---It {{KW|Channel|Channels}} 1 {{KW|Frost|Frost Orb}}, then draws 1 (2) card(s).--->\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n==== a) General Orb Synergies ====\n* Coolheaded works best with other Orb sources, such as {{C|Ball Lightning}} and {{C|Darkness}}, allowing Orbs to be {{KW|Evoke|Evoked}} more frequently. <!--- No idea what to include as prototypical orb gen cards, so just went with these two--->\n* {{C|Blizzard}} does more damage for each {{KW|Frost|Frost Orb}} {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} this combat.\n* Sources of {{BD|Focus}} will improve the effects of Orbs: {{C|Defragment}}, {{C|Consume}}, {{C|Biased Cognition}}, {{R|Data Disk}}\n* Sources of additional Orb Slots allow for having more [[Orbs#Passive|Orb Passives]] in parallel: {{C|Capacitor}}, {{R|Runic Capacitor}}, {{R|Inserter}}, {{P|Potion of Capacity}}\n* {{C|Compile Driver}} draws a card for each unique type of Orb {{KW|Channel|Channeled}}.\n* {{C|Barrage}} deals damage for each {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} Orb, while {{C|Fission}} draws a card and adds 1 {{Icon|BE}} for each Channeled Orb.\n* {{C|Recursion}}, {{C|Dualcast}}, and {{C|Multi-Cast}} each can directly {{KW|Evoke}} your Orbs 1, 2, or X times respectively.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{C|Reprogram}} and {{C|Hyperbeam}} give negative {{BD|Focus}}, making Orbs generated by Coolheaded less effective.\n\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2087":{"pageid":2087,"ns":0,"title":"Defragment","revisions":[{"revid":55735,"parentid":50584,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Defragment\n|Image       = Blue-Defragment.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Gain (1;2) {{BD|Focus}}.\n}}\n{{C|Defragment}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}}. <!---It applies 1 (2) {{BD|Focus}}.--->\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* In general, additive effects are applied before multiplicative ones. If a damaging Orb is improved by {{BD|Focus}} and then damages an enemy with {{BD|Lock-On}}, the {{BD|Focus}} will be added before the 50% increase from {{BD|Lock-On}}.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Like all sources of {{BD|Focus}}, Defragment improves the output of {{KW|Lightning}}, {{KW|Frost}}, and {{KW|Dark}} Orbs.\n* Sources of {{BD|Focus}} stack, so Defragment also works well with {{C|Consume}}, {{C|Biased Cognition}}, and {{R|Data Disk}}.\n* As increasing {{BD|Focus}} makes each of your non-{{KW|Plasma|Plasma Orbs}} better, sources of {{BD|Focus}} generally scale multiplicatively with sources of additional Orb Slots: {{C|Capacitor}}, {{R|Runic Capacitor}}, {{R|Inserter}}, {{P|Potion of Capacity}}.\n* {{C|Bullseye}} applies {{BD|Lock-On}}, which makes damaging Orbs deal 50% more damage to that enemy, and applies after {{BD|Focus}} for large damage output.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{KW|Plasma|Plasma Orbs}} are wholly unaffected by {{BD|Focus}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{C|Reprogram}} and {{C|Hyperbeam}} give negative {{BD|Focus}}, undoing the benefit of Defragment.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1941":{"pageid":1941,"ns":0,"title":"Disarm","revisions":[{"revid":56765,"parentid":55743,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Disarm\n|Image       = Red-Disarm.png\n|Color       = Red\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Enemy loses (2;3) {{BD|Strength}}.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|GivesToEnemy = Strength (Negative)\n}} \n{{Power Infobox|Strength}} \n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Disarm}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives '''negative''' 2 (3 if upgraded) {{BD|Strength}} to the target. {{C|Disarm}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]\n[[Category:ToUpdate]]"}}}]},"2091":{"pageid":2091,"ns":0,"title":"Electrodynamics","revisions":[{"revid":55755,"parentid":50620,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Electrodynamics\n|Image       = Blue-Electrodynamics.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = {{KW|Lightning}} now hits ALL enemies.<br>{{KW|Channel}} (2;3) {{KW|Lightning}}.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Electro}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Lightning}}\n{{C|Electrodynamics}} is a 2 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}}. <!---It makes damage dealt by {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}} hit ALL enemies, and then {{KW|Channel|Channels}} 2 (3) {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}}.--->\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* The {{BD|Electro}} [[Buff]] applies before the Orbs are {{KW|Channel|Channeled}}, so any {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}} {{KW|Evoke|Evoked}} by playing it will hit all enemies.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Electrodynamics makes all sources of {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}} much more effective in multi-enemy fights, especially cards like {{C|Tempest}}, {{C|Storm}}, and {{C|Static Discharge}}, which make several {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}}.\n** {{C|Thunder Strike}} hits more times for each {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}} {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} this combat, so it benefits from both Electrodynamics and the cards that it supports.\n\n==== a) General Orb Synergies ====\n* Other Orb sources, such as {{C|Darkness}} and {{C|Coolheaded}}, can be very helpful for {{KW|Evoke|Evoking}} {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}} more frequently.\n* Sources of {{BD|Focus}} will improve the effects of Orbs: {{C|Defragment}}, {{C|Consume}}, {{C|Biased Cognition}}, {{R|Data Disk}}\n* Sources of additional Orb Slots allow for having more [[Orbs#Passive|Orb Passives]] in parallel: {{C|Capacitor}}, {{R|Runic Capacitor}}, {{R|Inserter}}, {{P|Potion of Capacity}}\n* {{C|Bullseye}} applies {{BD|Lock-On}}, which makes damaging Orbs deal 50% more damage to that enemy.\n* {{C|Compile Driver}} draws a card for each unique type of Orb {{KW|Channel|Channeled}}.\n* {{C|Barrage}} deals damage for each {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} Orb, while {{C|Fission}} draws a card and adds 1 {{Icon|BE}} for each Channeled Orb.\n* {{C|Recursion}}, {{C|Dualcast}}, and {{C|Multi-Cast}} each can directly {{KW|Evoke}} your Orbs 1, 2, or X times respectively.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Playing multiple copies of Electrodynamics will not change the effect of {{BD|Electro}}, but you will still get the Orbs.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{C|Reprogram}} and {{C|Hyperbeam}} give negative {{BD|Focus}}, making {{KW|Lightning}} Orbs less effective.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 48: Creative AI'''\n** Electrodynamics' passively triggered Orbs now resolve in the correct order and flash the orbs\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1938":{"pageid":1938,"ns":0,"title":"Entrench","revisions":[{"revid":56763,"parentid":55760,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Entrench\n| Image       = Red-Entrench.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 2\n| CostPlus    = 1\n| Description = Double your {{KW|Block}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Block\n| InteractsWith = Block\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}}\n{{C|Entrench}} is a 2 (1 if upgraded) {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It doubles your current {{KW|Block}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* As it doubles existing {{KW|Block}} instead of giving {{KW|Block}} directly, {{C|Entrench}} is unaffected by {{BD|Frail}}, {{BD|Dexterity}} or {{BD|No Block}} from a previously played {{C|Panic Button}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 13: Thinking Ahead'''\n** We removed one level of unlocks! Three additional cards are now available by default in the card pool for both The Silent and Ironclad. The following cards are now added to the card pool by default: Ghostly Armor, Carnage, Entrench\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1877":{"pageid":1877,"ns":0,"title":"Flex","revisions":[{"revid":56413,"parentid":55783,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Flex\n| Image       = Red-Flex.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Common\n| Cost        = 0\n| Description = Gain (2;4) {{BD|Strength}}.<br>At the end of this turn, lose (2;4) {{BD|Strength}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Strength, Strength Down\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Strength}} {{Power Infobox|Strength Down}}\n{{C|Flex}} is a 0 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 2 (4 if upgraded) {{BD|Strength}} and gives the same amount of {{BD|Strength Down}} to remove that missing {{BD|Strength}} at the end of your turn.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* Both {{BD|Strength Down}} and the actual subtraction of that {{BD|Strength}} at the end of the turn are considered separate debuffs, meaning {{BD|Artifact}} can prevent either one. \n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Limit Break}} doubles your {{BD|Strength}} but does not affect {{BD|Strength Down}} so you will still only lose 2 (4 if upgraded) {{BD|Strength}} at the end of the turn, but the rest gained through {{C|Limit Break}} stays permanent.\n* {{R|Orange Pellets}} can remove the {{BD|Strength Down}} you get from this card, making the {{BD|Strength}} gain permanent.\n* Sources of {{BD|Artifact}}, such as {{R|Clockwork Souvenir}}, {{P|Ancient Potion}}, {{C|Core Surge}} and {{C|Panacea}} can prevent this card from applying {{BD|Strength Down}} or negate the {{BD|Strength}} removal at the end of your turn, and allow the {{BD|Strength}} gain to be permanent.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Since {{BD|Strength}} is capped to 999 while {{BD|Strength Down}} is effectively uncapped, it is possible to gain '''negative''' {{BD|Strength}} at the end of the turn, if {{C|Flex}} is played enough times in a single turn.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 24: Potions?!'''\n** Flex Power's downside Debuff renamed for clarity.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2464":{"pageid":2464,"ns":0,"title":"Mayhem","revisions":[{"revid":55854,"parentid":50744,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Mayhem\n|Image       = Colorless-Mayhem.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 2\n|CostPlus    = 1\n|Description = At the start of your turn, play the top card of your draw pile.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Mayhem}}{{C|Mayhem}} is a 2 (1 if upgraded) {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives one {{BD|Mayhem}}, which plays the top card of your draw pile at the start of every turn, without expending any {{Icon|CE}} '''Energy'''. X-cost cards will use your current {{Icon|CE}} '''Energy''' for X, without consuming that {{Icon|CE}} '''Energy'''.\n\n== Obtaining Mayhem ==\n{{C|Mayhem}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]], [[Elites]] and [[Bosses]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[Third Blessing]] in exchange for a negative effect.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{BD|Mayhem}} activates ''after'' drawing cards at the start of the turn, meaning that something that is placed on top of your draw pile at the end of your previous turn will not be played through {{BD|Mayhem}} but drawn as normal.\n* If you have {{BD|Echo Form}}, the card played by {{C|Mayhem}} will be played twice by that {{BD|Echo Form}} and consume it for that turn.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Frozen Eye}} allows you to see which card {{C|Mayhem}} will target.\n* {{C|Mayhem}} will play X-cost cards for their full {{Icon|CE}} '''Energy''' without actually using any.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Playing a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} or {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} card via {{BD|Mayhem}} will place the card into your discard pile, bypassing end-of-turn negative effects from cards such as {{C|Doubt}} and {{C|Burn}}, but also preventing {{KW|Ethereal}} cards such as {{C|Ascender's Bane}} and {{C|Dazed}} from being {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}}.\n** If you have {{R|Medical Kit}} or {{R|Blue Candle}}, respectively {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} or {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} will be {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} when they are played by {{BD|Mayhem}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* Generally, there is little control over which card is played by {{BD|Mayhem}}. This means cards with possible negative effects, such as {{C|Offering}}, {{C|Eruption}} or {{C|Blasphemy}} can be played, or cards that need to be played at a specific time for maximum effect, such as {{C|Limit Break}} or {{C|Apparition}} can be wasted.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** Fixed Mayhem, Havoc, Distilled Chaos, and Omniscience sometimes not playing cards if original target is dead.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Accuracy power now correctly works with Shivs played from the top of the deck via cards like Mayhem or Havoc.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 47: Metamorphosis'''\n** Fixed bug where playing Mayhem card would alter your card rewards.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 38: Bane'''\n** Adding colorless card Mayhem.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2042":{"pageid":2042,"ns":0,"title":"Nightmare","revisions":[{"revid":55870,"parentid":50539,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Nightmare\n|Image       = Green-Nightmare.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 3\n|CostPlus    = 2\n|Description = Choose a card.<br>Next turn, add 3 copies of that card into your hand. {{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|Keywords    = Hand\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Nightmare}}{{C|Nightmare}} is a 3 (2 if upgraded) {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* When a card is copied, any alterations to that card are also copied, where the duration of these alterations is the same for the copy as for the original. After being copied, these cards behave fully independently. The alterations that are copied include but are not limited to:\n** A changed energy cost through something like {{R|Snecko Eye}}, {{C|Madness}} or {{P|Liquid Memories}}, or the automatic energy change of cards like {{C|Blood for Blood}} and {{C|Masterful Stab}}.\n** Changes to the values of the card, such as upgrades to {{C|Searing Blow}} or increased damage of {{C|Windmill Strike}}.\n* Changes that last for one turn, such as an energy discount through {{C|Bullet Time}} or the energy discount of {{C|Eviscerate}} are not copied.\n\n* If a copy created by this exceeds the hand size limit, it gets added to the discard pile.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Internally called Night_Terror.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Updating icon for Nightmare power.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 9: Ascension'''\n** Nightmare no longer retains \"cost for turn\" when copying cards (as you get the copies next turn).\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Nightmare+ card is nerfed. No longer adds 4 cards, just lowers energy cost.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 6: We're Back!'''\n** New green card, Nightmare. Description withheld for spoiler reasons.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1950":{"pageid":1950,"ns":0,"title":"Parasite","revisions":[{"revid":56774,"parentid":55892,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Parasite\n| Image       = Curse-Parasite.png\n| Color       = Colorless\n| Type        = Curse\n| Cost        = -2\n| NoUpgrade   = true\n| Description = {{KW|Unplayable}}.<br>If transformed or removed from your deck, lose 3 Max HP.\n| GivesToPlayer = Unplayable\n| InteractsWith = Transform\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Unplayable}}\n{{C|Parasite}} is an {{KW|Unplayable}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} Card. If Parasite is {{KW|Transform|Transformed}} or [[Merchant#Card Removal Service|Removed]] from your deck, you will lose 3 Max HP immediately.\n\n== Obtaining Parasite ==\nLike most {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curses}}, Parasite can be obtained from anything that gives a random Curse:\n* Can be part of Neow's [[Third Blessing]] in exchange for a reward.\n* {{E|Match and Keep}}.\n* {{R|Cursed Key}}.\n* {{KW|Transform|Transforming}} another Curse.\n\nIn addition, Parasite can be obtained from both the {{E|Hypnotizing Colored Mushrooms}} Event and the {{M|Writhing Mass}} fight. It is the only card in the game which can be added to your deck permanently mid-combat.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\nAs Parasite is a '''{{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}}''', it interacts with the following:\n* {{C|Fire Breathing}} will deal damage when it is drawn.\n* {{R|Du-Vu Doll}} will give you 1 {{BD|Strength}} each combat.\n* {{R|Blue Candle}} can be used to {{KW|Exhaust}} it for 1 HP. \n** Note that Exhausting Parasite does ''not'' trigger the Max HP loss.\n* When added to the deck, it will be negated by {{R|Omamori}}, or gain you 6 max HP if you have {{R|Darkstone Periapt}} and ''not'' Omamori.\n\nWays to gain more Max HP repeatedly will make the downside of removing Parasite minimal:\n* {{C|Feed}} can gain you Max HP when you kill enemies with it.\n* {{R|Singing Bowl}} can gain you Max HP whenever you skip a card reward.\n\nSomewhat counterintuitively, reducing your Max HP once can make other Max HP reduction Events slightly better, as most Events that reduce your Max HP do so as a percentage of your current Max HP.\n* For instance, say you have 75 Max HP, and then remove a Parasite, leaving you with 72 HP. Then, you encounter the {{E|Council of Ghosts}} Event, which allows you to pay half of your Max HP for 5 ({{Asc|15|3}}) copies of {{C|Apparition}}. From 72 Max HP, this would be a payment of 36 Max HP, for a total of 39 Max HP lost. If instead you had not removed the Parasite, you would be asked to pay 38 Max HP, only 1 less total, while keeping the Curse.\n\n=== Neutral ===\nLike all sources of Max HP loss, Parasite:\n* Won't affect your current HP, unless you have less HP than your new Maximum, in which case it will also lower to the same amount.\n* Cannot lower your Max HP below 1. If it would, it sets it to 1 instead.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As {{C|Clash}} can only be played when all cards in your hand are {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}}, if it is drawn at the same time as Parasite, it cannot be played.\n* While it is often still worthwhile to remove Parasite with things such as {{R|Empty Cage}}, doing so will reduce your Max HP by 3.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* As most Curses are only given in a single Event (not counting random ones), Parasite is tied with {{C|Writhe}} and {{C|Regret}} for being the Curse with the most ways to get it.\n* {{M|Writhing Mass}} is the only thing in the game which can permanently add a card to your deck mid combat. In addition, there are a number of ways to affect your game state in a lasting way mid combat ({{C|Hand of Greed}}, {{C|Alchemize}}), but they are nearly all player-controlled. The only enemies which can cause such things to happen (aside from HP loss) are Writhing Mass and the {{M|Looter}} and {{M|Mugger}}, who can steal your [[Gold]].\n* This card's [[Beta Art]] shows the parasite causing the terrible affliction of :3 to the [[Ironclad]], [[Silent]], and [[Defect]].\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2295":{"pageid":2295,"ns":0,"title":"Protect","revisions":[{"revid":54830,"parentid":50651,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Protect\n|Image       = Purple-Protect.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = {{KW|Retain}}.<br>Gain (12;16) {{KW|Block}}.\n}}\n{{C|Protect}} is a 2 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 12 (16 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}}. It has {{KW|Retain}}, meaning it will not be discarded when you end your turn.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* As it {{KW|Retain|Retains}}, {{C|Establishment}} will decrease it in {{Icon|PE}}-cost at the end of a turn, unless it already costs 0.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2423":{"pageid":2423,"ns":0,"title":"Sanctity","revisions":[{"revid":50677,"parentid":36405,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Sanctity\n|Image       = Purple-Sanctity.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Gain (6;9) {{KW|Block}}. <br>If the last card played this combat was a Skill, draw 2 cards.\n|Keywords    = Draw\n}}\n{{C|Sanctity}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It gives 6 (9 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}}. If the last card played this combat was a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}}, this also draws 2 cards.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1849":{"pageid":1849,"ns":0,"title":"Seeing Red","revisions":[{"revid":56398,"parentid":53363,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Seeing Red\n| Image       = Red-SeeingRed.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 1\n| CostPlus    = 0\n| Description = Gain {{Icon|RE}} {{Icon|RE}}.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Exhaust, Energy\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Seeing Red}} is a 1 (0) {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 2 {{Icon|RE}} '''Energy'''. {{C|Seeing Red}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2260":{"pageid":2260,"ns":0,"title":"Self Repair","revisions":[{"revid":55934,"parentid":50605,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Self Repair\n|Image       = Blue-SelfRepair.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = At the end of combat, heal (7;10) HP.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Repair}}{{C|Self Repair}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 7 (10 if upgraded) {{BD|Repair}}, which will heal you for that amount of HP at the end of combat.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* Healing cards cannot be generated mid-combat to avoid infinite healing, so {{C|Self Repair}} cannot be created by {{C|White Noise}} or {{R|Dead Branch}}. \n** However, if you already have a {{C|Self Repair}}, ways to increase the amount of {{C|Self Repair|Self Repairs}} played, like {{C|Amplify}} and {{C|Dual Wield}} can still be generated, allowing you to heal for more anyway.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** All sources of random temporary card generation in combat (like Dead Branch) can no longer generate cards that provide healing.\n** New tip added to indicate that healing cards cannot be generated randomly during combat.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1452":{"pageid":1452,"ns":0,"title":"Strike (Watcher)","revisions":[{"revid":50631,"parentid":43238,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Strike (Watcher)\n|DisplayName = Strike\n|Image       = Purple-Strike.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Basic\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (6;9) damage.\n}}\n{{C|Strike (Watcher)|Strike}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Basic|Basic}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 6 (9 if upgraded) damage.\n\nThis page is for Watcher's version of Strike. Go here for {{C|Strike (Ironclad)}}, {{C|Strike (Silent)}}, {{C|Strike (Defect)}}\n\n== Obtaining Strike ==\nThe [[Watcher]] starts with 4 copies of {{C|Strike (Watcher)|Strike}} in her deck. It cannot be obtained through regular card rewards.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Strike (Watcher)|Strike}} gets a damage increase of 3 from {{R|Strike Dummy}}, and adds to the damage of {{C|Perfected Strike}}.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1533":{"pageid":1533,"ns":0,"title":"Wild Strike","revisions":[{"revid":50408,"parentid":35941,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Wild Strike\n|Image       = Red-WildStrike.png\n|Color       = Red\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (12;17) damage.<br>Shuffle a {{C|Wound}} into your draw pile.\n}}\n{{Small Card Infobox|Wound}}\n{{C|Wild Strike}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 12 (17 when upgraded) damage and adds a {{C|Wound}} into your draw pile.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order === \n* The {{C|Wound}} gets added into your draw pile ''before'' triggering {{R|Ink Bottle}}.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Synergizes with {{C|Fire Breathing}} and {{C|Evolve}}, as it creates a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} card in your draw pile.\n* {{C|Wild Strike}} gets a damage increase of 3 from {{R|Strike Dummy}}, and adds to the damage of {{C|Perfected Strike}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 21: Channel Lightning'''\n** Wild Strike card is now Common.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 20: Immolate'''\n** Wild Strike card is now Uncommon.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1907":{"pageid":1907,"ns":0,"title":"Writhe","revisions":[{"revid":56435,"parentid":56008,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Writhe\n| Image       = Curse-Writhe.png\n| Color       = Colorless\n| Type        = Curse\n| Cost        = -2\n| NoUpgrade   = true\n| Description = {{KW|Unplayable}}.<br>{{KW|Innate}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Unplayable, Innate\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Unplayable}} {{Keyword Infobox|Innate}}\n{{C|Writhe}} is an {{KW|Unplayable}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} Card. It is {{KW|Innate}}.\n\n== Obtaining Writhe ==\nLike most {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curses}}, Writhe can be obtained from anything that gives a random Curse:\n* Can be part of Neow's [[Third Blessing]] in exchange for a reward.\n* {{E|Match and Keep}}.\n* {{R|Cursed Key}}.\n* {{KW|Transform|Transforming}} another Curse.\n\nIn addition, Writhe can be obtained from two events:\n* {{E|The Mausoleum}} when choosing {{Frame|Open Coffin}}.\n* {{E|Winding Halls}} when choosing {{Frame|Pass On}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\nAs Writhe is a '''{{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}}''', it interacts with the following:\n* {{C|Fire Breathing}} will deal damage when it is drawn.\n* {{R|Du-Vu Doll}} will give you 1 {{BD|Strength}} each combat.\n* {{R|Blue Candle}} can be used to {{KW|Exhaust}} it for 1 HP. \n* When added to the deck, it will be negated by {{R|Omamori}}, or gain you 6 max HP if you have {{R|Darkstone Periapt}} and ''not'' {{R|Omamori}}.\n\nAs Writhe is '''{{KW|Innate}}''', the downside of having it can be mitigated:\n* {{R|Gambling Chip}} allows you to discard it away at the start of combat, meaning you won't draw it until after the first shuffle.\n* {{R|Ring of the Snake}} and {{R|Bag of Preparation}} both draw you additional cards on your first turn, lessening the impact of an Innate curse in your starting hand.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As {{C|Clash}} can only be played when all cards in your hand are {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}}, if it is drawn at the same time as Writhe, it cannot be played.\n\n== Trivia ==\nAs most Curses are only given in a single Event (not counting random ones), Writhe is tied with {{C|Parasite}} and {{C|Regret}} for being the Curse with the most ways to get it.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]}}}}